IMPORT prelude
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §11.0.1, "Stacking B on C (2026-09-16)": the
-- anchored WITHIN (R-Q7B, §5.1.1.1) on top of the blame set (R-T3, §6.1.1).
--
-- C: a barrier's LEST fires ONCE for the group, anchored at the EARLIEST
-- failure by R-Q5 — the member's act deadline for MUST/DO/MAY, the violating
-- stamp for SHANT — with that member's residual stream. B: a continuation
-- reads THE DEADLINE from the obligation it is attached to; under a
-- barrier's LEST that is the deadline a member missed.
--
-- Stacked, these must name the SAME member: THE DEADLINE under a barrier's
-- LEST is the deadline of the member whose failure the LEST is anchored at
-- — the earliest failure — wherever that member stands on the roll. Two
-- failures at the same stamp are ordered by the stream first (two SHANT
-- violations at one stamp are two events, and the LEST gets the residual
-- of the one the stream reached first), then by the deadline missed (two
-- misses the same event revealed), and only then by roll position, which by
-- then names the same anchor, residual and deadline either way. Every trace
-- below pins the number that rule produces, for each of the four modals
-- (MUST §1-3, MAY §3b, DO §3c, SHANT §4-4b); the comment says what a
-- different rule would have produced instead.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Refund  HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Smoke   HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Approve HAS who    IS AN Actor

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
carol       MEANS Tenant OF "Carol"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob, carol
`tenants, reversed` MEANS LIST carol, bob, alice

-- Carol, LAST on the roll, has the EARLIEST deadline (5); Bob, before her,
-- has 14; Alice too.
GIVEN t IS AN Actor
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days allowed to` t MEANS IF t EQUALS carol THEN 5 ELSE 14


§ `1. the last member on the roll fails first: THE DEADLINE is hers`

-- Alice signs at 1. Carol misses 5 (revealed by WAIT UNTIL 8); Bob misses
-- 14 (revealed by WAIT UNTIL 20). The LEST is anchored at Carol's failure
-- (revealed at 8, before Bob's at 20), and THE DEADLINE under it is CAROL's,
-- 5: the refund is due 5 + 5 = 10. A refund at 10 is timely; at 11 the
-- breach reports 10. Were THE DEADLINE Bob's — first on the roll to fail,
-- 14 — the refund would be due 19 and both refunds would be timely.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`staggered` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MUST   Sign t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `2. the roll reversed: the same member, the same deadline`

-- Carol is now FIRST on the roll. Same events, same answer: due 10.
#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `3. a tie: both misses revealed by the SAME event`

-- Nothing happens between Carol's deadline (5) and Bob's (14): WAIT UNTIL 20
-- reveals both at once. The LEST's anchor (the revealing stamp, 20) and its
-- residual stream are the same whichever member is chosen, so for the blame
-- set alone the tie did not matter; THE DEADLINE is 5 or 14 depending on
-- it. The earliest failure by R-Q5 is Carol's (5 < 14) from either roll, so
-- the tie is broken by the deadline missed and the refund at 21 reports
-- 5 + 5 = 10 on BOTH rolls. (Broken by roll order it reported 19 on
-- `tenants` and 10 on `tenants, reversed` — measured 2026-09-16 before the
-- tie-break was added.)
#TRACE `staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

#TRACE `staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21


§ `3b. MAY: the permission that expires first anchors the LEST, and THE DEADLINE is its window's end`

-- The three shapes above, with MAY members. A permission its holder does
-- not exercise expires at its deadline (R-Q5's act layer: MUST, DO and MAY
-- all fail at the deadline), and under a barrier that has a LEST the
-- expiry is a failure the LEST is anchored at, exactly as a MUST member's
-- miss is. Alice approves at 1. Carol's permission (window 5) expires
-- unexercised, revealed by WAIT UNTIL 8; Bob's (14) by WAIT UNTIL 20. THE
-- DEADLINE under the LEST is Carol's 5, so the refund is due 10: at 10
-- FULFILLED, at 11 BREACHED reporting 10, on both rolls. The tie — WAIT
-- UNTIL 20 reveals both expiries at once — is broken by the deadline,
-- 5 < 14: the refund at 21 reports 10 on both rolls. When everybody
-- approves in time the join fires: FULFILLED.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`may approve` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        MAY    Approve t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `may approve` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `may approve` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `may approve` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `may approve` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

#TRACE `may approve` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 21

#TRACE `may approve` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Approve alice AT 1
  PARTY carol DOES Approve carol AT 2
  PARTY bob   DOES Approve bob   AT 3


§ `3c. DO: as MUST`

-- DO is the bare form, and behaves as MUST does: a DO member's miss is
-- revealed and ordered exactly as a MUST member's. Carol misses 5,
-- revealed by WAIT UNTIL 8; THE DEADLINE under the LEST is hers, so the
-- refund is due 10: at 10 FULFILLED, at 11 BREACHED reporting 10, on both
-- rolls.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`do staggered` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        DO     Sign t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `do staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `do staggered` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `do staggered` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 1
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 8)
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `4. SHANT: the violating stamp orders, the window's end is THE DEADLINE`

-- A prohibition barrier. Carol's window ends at 5, Bob's at 14. Carol smokes
-- at 3 (failure time 3 by R-Q5), Bob at 10 (failure time 10); Alice keeps
-- hers. The LEST is anchored at Carol's violation (3 < 10) and THE DEADLINE
-- under it is Carol's window end, 5 — what a single SHANT's LEST is handed
-- — so the refund is due 5 + 5 = 10: at 10 FULFILLED, at 11 BREACHED
-- reporting 10. The same on the reversed roll.
GIVEN roll IS A LIST OF Actor
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no smoking` roll MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN roll
        SHANT  Smoke t
        WITHIN `days allowed to` t
        ONCE   ALL HAVE
        HENCE  FULFILLED
        LEST   (PARTY theLandlord MUST Refund theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)

#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 10
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 10
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)


§ `4b. SHANT at one stamp: two events, two residuals — the stream orders`

-- Bob (window 14) and Carol (window 5) BOTH smoke at 3, Bob's event first,
-- and the landlord refunds at 3 BETWEEN the two violations. Two failures
-- at one stamp, but two different events: Bob's residual stream still holds
-- the refund, Carol's does not. The LEST is anchored at the failure the
-- stream reached first — Bob's — so THE DEADLINE is his window end, 14, the
-- refund is due 19, and the refund at 3 discharges it: FULFILLED, on both
-- rolls. (Ordered by the window's end instead — Carol's 5 — the refund
-- would be dropped from the residual and the verdict BREACHED at 20
-- reporting 10, on both rolls: measured 2026-09-16 before the stream key
-- was added. Ordered by the roll, FULFILLED on `tenants` and BREACHED on
-- `tenants, reversed`: the blame set alone, measured on its own branch.)
#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 3
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 3
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

-- The same two violations with the refund AFTER both. Bob's failure is
-- still the first in the stream, so THE DEADLINE is 14 and the refund is
-- due 19: at 11 FULFILLED; at 20 BREACHED reporting 19, on both rolls.
-- (By the window's end the refund would be due 10: the one at 11 BREACHED
-- reporting 10.)
#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 3
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 11
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)

#TRACE `no smoking` tenants AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 3
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20

#TRACE `no smoking` `tenants, reversed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY bob   DOES Smoke bob   AT 3
  PARTY carol DOES Smoke carol AT 3
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Refund theLandlord AT 20


§ `5. RAND of two anchored continuations, both breached`

-- Alice signs at 4: the join is 4, THE DEADLINE 10. The landlord's delivery
-- is due 10 + 5 = 15 (OF THE DEADLINE); Bob's signature 4 + 3 = 7 (OF THE
-- JOIN). Neither happens; WAIT UNTIL 20 reveals both at once. The RAND is
-- anchored at the first breach — a tie at 20, so the LEFT operand — and it
-- names BOTH failures, left first, each with the deadline its anchor
-- produced: the landlord's 15, then Bob's 7.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both anchored` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign alice WITHIN 10
    HENCE ((PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver theLandlord WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
           RAND (PARTY bob MUST Sign bob WITHIN 3 OF THE JOIN))
    LEST  BREACH

#TRACE `both anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  (`WAIT UNTIL` 20)
